RT @HungarySzoboFPL: 🐝 Hivemind notes 🐝

For this season, a small group (now 8) have banded together for the @Jumpthewave predictions to have a group think each GW. 

Everyone is set on the back 4 once again. Midfield too. The front line is where things differ and that is, as I mentioned above, between Gakpo and Ngumoha. 

Some paraphrased comments from the predicting team: 

@FPL__Lad - “It is absolutely battering it down here. Wind is crazy.”

“There's every chance Rio gets a start after that very impressive midweek performance but if Gakpo and Barcola are both fully fit I just see it being those two. Isak leading the line after a fair amount of rest.”

@FPL_Baldie - “It’s good to note that we have had 4 days rest for this one so I can see Gakpo going again for Brighton. He’s the most accustomed to to this schedule after all but yeah, I think Rio is better off the right, so I think the 50/50 here is Gakpo/Barcola.”

@thomas_toner22 - “Chance Gakpo starts but think the fact he played 90 after an injury and Rio came off with 20 to go and played so well, I think he starts again on the right.”

@YashAsthana87 - once again, the team graphic is all him 💪🏼

